Phase 18 assignment attachment nullable-key parity
Date: 2026-10-23
Branch: phase/18-phase-18-compatibility-closure
Pinned Java: RocketMQ client 5.5.1, source commit efa1be59d6fc747ad220f036c86030f05f0419f9

Java probe: `MessageQueueAssignment.setAttachments` accepts a map with a null
key; `getAttachments` returns the same map. Fastjson serializes the null key
as the property name `"null"`, omits null-valued entries, and emits duplicate
`"null"` properties when a literal `"null"` key coexists with the null key.

Rust change: `AssignmentAttachments` represents nullable keys with
`Option<String>` and retains the shared setter/getter map handle. JSON input
property `"null"` remains a string key; output maps the null key to `"null"`.
Snapshots retain null values while the assignment DTO encoder omits them.
Java oracle was added to `fixtures/runtime/lookup.json` as
`assignmentNullAttachmentApiCase`.

Implementation commit: 5dffd30b (fix: preserve null assignment attachment keys)
Lookup fixture SHA-256: 42af689aed0d150ee19fef5d8138627bb09db9085139b5221d579e57a0053283

